arget=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:20:25-07:00","id":1401686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1401678#post1401678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Moncada.<br /> <br /> Lucita's abusive pervert of a sire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that's what I suspected. I didn't know he has True Faith, I thought only Anatole has it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:56:53-07:00","id":1401795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1401678#post1401678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Moncada.<br /> <br /> Lucita's abusive pervert of a sire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he's usually the first thing I think of when I consider the idea that non-mortals maybe shouldn't have access to True Faith. (I've long considered that ability to be kind of broken on a number of levels, but that's probably a discussion for another thread.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T18:32:55-07:00","id":1401818,"title":"","content":"<b>The Inquisition (part three)</b><br /> <br /> And our final two. <br /> <br /> <b>The Quisling </b><br /> A vampire ghoul who infiltrated the Society at the behest of his master. We don't really get much in the way of backstory or the like, aside from that he was able to attract the Inquisition's attention by setting up one of his master's enemies. However, we do get a pretty interesting look at his inner psychology. Part of this is that he &quot;willingly&quot; became a ghoul out of love for his master, which ties in with what we were discussing earlier regarding how Presence can screw with matters of consent and free will among its victims. Also, and I presume this is a reflection of having to spend so much time away from the master, but one could also decide to interpret it as perhaps some sort of divine influence, he keeps having these internal doubts, wondering why Master seems so distant and doesn't seem to care much about his safety. I actually find this to be a nice touch, and in hindsight wish that one or more of the Ghoul templates had done this also. Mental is primary, all at three. I've no idea if Physicals or Socials are meant to be secondary, as at least two extra dots have been purchased with freebies, resulting in Dexterity, Stamina, and Manipulation all at three. Firearms is at four dots, and Brawl and Dodge are at three. Acting, Alertness, Athletics, Melee, Security, Bureaucracy and Computer are at two. I find myself wishing that there'd been a stronger focus on the abilities used for being a deep cover spy than the usual collection of combat ones. Stuff like Subterfuge, Investigation, or Stealth. No Numina, per say, but he has one dot of Potence. Backgrounds include two each in Allies, Contacts (Outside), and Resources, and one each in Mentor (Kindred) and Status. Humanity is seven and Willpower is four (the lowest in this book). Overall, this is a pretty interesting idea for an Inquisition character, and one I probably wouldn't have thought of on my own. My only real issues are that I wish I knew more about him as an individual instead of just as a ghoul, and that I wish his skills were a little different. (I'll also point out that the character sheet doesn't add up. With ten freebies spent on extra attributes, six on abilities, three on backgrounds, and none on Humanity or WP, that leaves all of two points for that dot of Potence. I'll also note that the art is particularly terrible, having very long hair flying straight up in the air and an arm that not only seems to reach past his knee, but also has an extra joint between the elbow and wrist.) <br /> <br /> <b>The Young Turk</b><br /> So, if our earlier <i>Gladius Dei</i> aspirant was a fairly straight arrow, this is essentially that turned on its head. A high school drop out and petty criminal with a lifelong distain for authority. Then what sounds like it was probably a half-assed effort at gay bashing (it's written rather vaguely, but involves him and his friends hassling a &quot;pretty boy&quot; at a bar) ended with his friends killed by a vampire and him seeking sanctuary in a church. The priest allowed him to stay there for a few weeks and eventually talked him into joining the Society. Unfortunately, his distain for authority and discipline make him something of a problem child. So he's kind of got that whole Lone Wolf McEdgelord thing going on. Physicals, naturally, are primary, with an extra dot to bump Stamina up to four. Mental is secondary, with Wits also at three. His abilities are pretty combat focused, but ironically a little more restrained than some of the others. Alertness, Brawl, Firearms, and Melee are all three. Athletics, Dodge, Stealth, and Occult are two. And then a few ones, which include Acting, Computer, and Politics. No Numina (making it so half the templates are normals and half have powers). Backgrounds include four dots in Mentor (the single highest background in this book), and one each in Allies, Resources, and Status. Humanity and Willpower are both at seven. The art is extremely crude, and he looks like he's trying for some sort of paramilitary look, including what has to be one of the worst efforts to draw an UZI I've seen since ... well, when I last tried to draw one. I'm not a huge fan of this one. The idea of a low-life turned vampire hunter is a good idea, but I think the execution could be a lot better. A (very) lapsed Catholic who has rediscovered his faith in the face of real monsters and now tries to put his criminal skills to use for the Inquisition sounds like a potentially interesting character to play. But this isn't really that character. Instead, it's one of those characters that seems likely to turn into a problem when he keeps insisting on acting like a jerkass. <br /> <br /> So, that's our Inquisitors. Overall, they're pretty decent. The ideas are all good ones, but a few of them wobble in the execution. The Young Turk is probably my least favorite, and I really do wish the Puritan had been a Catholic with True Faith instead. The Quisling wins for &quot;idea I'd not have thought of on my own&quot;. <br /> Representation .... They are all men. And all white, at least as near as I can tell given the poor artwork. I find this rather mind-boggling. Back when this book came out, WWGS was really at the forefront of the gaming industry in showcasing female characters. I realize that there is this weird tendency to try to stereotype the Catholic Church and faith based witch hunters as a male thing, but the book does devote a fair amount of attention to the issue of women in the Inquisition, including two different orders of nuns and two previous leaders of the entire Society. And I find the lack of Latin characters very odd. <br /> What's missing? Well, a nun would've been nice. One with True Faith, or with the healing Theurgy power, or with prophetic ability. And at least one other female character. I also would've liked to see at least one Investigation oriented character. The stereotype of Irish, Italian and Latin police officers from major metropolitan cities makes me wonder how it was skipped. (If you ever saw the 90s tv series Homicide: Life on the Streets, Andre Braugher's character of Frank Pembleton was a Catholic who attended a Jesuit high school in NYC, and in addition to being an excellent detective and interrogator was also knowledgable in Greek, Latin and Catholic theology. I have long thought he'd have made a very interesting member of the Inquisition.) I also think it would've been interesting to see an Inquisitor who was focused on the Christian idea of mercy and redemption, as sort of a forerunner to the Redeemer creed from Hunter the Reckoning.<br /> <br /> (Of the hunter books, I think this is the one that probably could've most benefited from a sequel - an Inquisition Companion or something - that gave chapter length treatments on the various non-Catholic faith based groups, like the Orthodox Akritai, the Muslim Brethren of Purity, and others.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's it for this book. Next, I will finally be talking about the Ravnos, and then the final book, the Giovanni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T23:25:28-07:00","id":1401862,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Weird how the game stresses True Faith is way more often found in generous, kind-hearted people than cruel butchers yet they keep writing characters who are anything but kind. Or maybe I'm just getting the wrong picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T02:43:03-07:00","id":1401878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1401862#post1401862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Weird how the game stresses True Faith is way more often found in generous, kind-hearted people than cruel butchers yet they keep writing characters who are anything but kind. Or maybe I'm just getting the wrong picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really liked the Vampyr game's most faithful priest. Ironically, he gets bitten by a vampire because he doesn't believe God would drive away a vampire as he loves all people.<br /> <br /> (Crosses explicitly can be used against the undead in the setting)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T06:25:51-07:00","id":1401912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1401862#post1401862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Weird how the game stresses True Faith is way more often found in generous, kind-hearted people than cruel butchers yet they keep writing characters who are anything but kind. Or maybe I'm just getting the wrong picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of it may have been it sort of being treated as a superpower to give certain npcs instead of as something that really needed an examination of both the game's cosmology and of the specific faith in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T14:57:51-07:00","id":1402124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1401555#post1401555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird. For some reason I was remembering Dane as a Puritan, probably because Solomon Kane was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he got mixed up in your memory with Righteous Endeavor, that Tzimisce former witch hunter? I know I've confused them at times. (It's the hat.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T19:51:42-07:00","id":1403325,"title":"","content":"<b>Clanbook: Ravnos (part one)</b><br /> <br /> Finally getting around to this. So, this book was still in the &quot;bad old days&quot; when the Ravnos clan was very much a bunch of stereotypical The Rom. And this book goes hard core into that, including using a bunch of stuff from the much maligned (deservedly so) WOD: Gypsies. This includes the total BS &quot;history&quot; of the The Rom with them originating in the First City and getting more &quot;please stop&quot; from there. This is also when the clan weakness was full on Cryme Tyme. Quite frankly, it's a miracle that all seven of these templates aren't toxic dumpster fires. <br /> So, this book was written by Christopher Walters, whose name I'm not familiar with from anything else. It was developed by Robert Hatch, who also did &quot;additional material&quot;. The art is, somewhat to my surprise, by Christopher Shy. This is well before his &quot;Celtic facial tattoos&quot; phase from Vampire's revised era, and when he's not doing weird ass photoshop effects, he's actually a pretty good artist. <br /> And this one once again does that annoying thing where the Concept on the character sheet is different from that of the write up's title. <br /> <br /> <b>The Ace of Spades (Natural Born Killer)</b><br /> So right out of the gate, we get a serial killer. Basically a sociopath from birth, somewhat obsessed with chance, a habitual liar, and a torturer or small animals, as an adult he graduated to killing people. Apparently he worked for the mob for a little while, but got bored with it and, after rolling some dice, killed all his employers. Then some Ravnos came along and embraced him. Now he just has more interesting ways to kill people, and will eventually work up to killing other vampires, werewolves, etc. Mental is primary, with a 3/3/4 split. Physicals are secondary, with an extra dot from freebies worked into Dexterity (the KillNinja attribute) for a 3/4/2 split. Charisma is one so that Manipulation can be three. Ability-wise, Firearms and Melee are both four dots, with Stealth at three. Alertness, Brawl, Dodge, Intimidation, Streetwise, Subterfuge, Computer and Investigation are all two dots. Disciplines are two dots in Chimerstry and one in Fortitude. Backgrounds are one in Contacts, three in Generation, and two in Resources. (No Mentor, so no idea what happened to his sire; Maybe he flipped a coin and killed him.) He's on the Path of Paradox, the special Ravnos path of enlightenment introduced in the second ed Players Guide. As my copy is in danger of falling apart, I can't really consult it, but it was one of those that I remember had a strong reputation of being a &quot;path of doing whatever I want&quot; deals. Anyway, he's got that at six, and is the only one in the book on that path. His Willpower is seven. The art work is pretty good, even if it's got that whole trench coat and long hair (and bare chest) thing going on that makes it a contender for The Most 90s-est 90s Thing to Have Ever 90s. I'm kind of on the fence about this character. One the pro side, he's not one of the The Rom. And his Cryme Tyme of Choice is at least sort of interesting. His stats are OK (and I get the sense that before becoming a full on killer for hire, he may have been an office drone of some sort, which I honestly would've found an interesting angle to explore more). On the con side, well, he's a serial killer, which is a little old hat at this point. And he's also very much a Lone Wolf who doesn't look like he'd have much interest in joining a coterie (unless his die roll came up a certain way) or working well with others. I think this one could probably be reworked a little into a much stronger character. Maybe as a Sabbat member who was a cube farm worker before getting snatched up and is now kind of obsessed with randomness and chance when he's the only survivor of the bunch of shovel heads he was created along side. Or perhaps someone who did enforcement work for the mob but didn't really enjoy it but now finds himself compelled to hurt and kill people. <br /> <br /> <b>The Carjacker (Young Thug)</b><br /> F&amp;@$ you, book. Sigh. So carjacking was one of those things from the 90s that the news media loved to talk about in its &quot;if it bleeds, it leads&quot; mentality. Usually part and parcel with all the talk about the coming wave of young &quot;super predator&quot; criminals (meaning young black males from the inner city). So this is a racial stereotype of that era in a book that's already got that problem coming out of its ears. But in a fit of irony, this character is not terrible. He's got a decent back story - the son of a Miami mechanic who picked up some of his father's skills, but decided to use them for easy money instead of honest work - and got recruited into the Sabbat after pissing off what's clearly meant to be the Setites (which ties back into the Voodoo priest from that book, interestingly enough). He acts like a total stereotype when he's relaxed but when getting ready to do a job becomes a lot more serious and professional. (While the art work is technically good, the fact that its a stereotypical looking black youth with a gun and a pair of pantyhose on his head makes me hate it.) Physicals are primary, with Strength and Dexterity at four. Mental is secondary with a 3/2/3 split. Drive is at four dots. Brawl, Intimidation, Repair and Security are all at three. Streetwise and Firearms are both at two (you'd think that first one would be higher), as is the secondary ability of Military Science (and wow has it been a while since I've seen that one). No idea where he picked that up. I guess from the rest of his pack. Disciplines are one in Chimerstry, two in Fortitude, and one in Celerity. No idea why he has the dot of Special Sauce, other than the fact that every character in the book has at least one, because I guess they have to. Backgrounds are two in Contacts and three in Herd. He's on the Path of Honorable Accord at five and has a Willpower of six. I don't think he spent all of his freebies, as two seem to be MIA. Obviously, his Cryme Tyme of Choice is stealing cars. As I said, this is not a terrible character, mostly owing to the effort put into his back story, but he really could be a lot better. The idea of a car thief - especially a Sabbat one - is a pretty good idea. But I wish it had avoided the &quot;urban super predator&quot; stereotype angle and gone for someone who was good enough not to have to resort to violence. Even better if his compulsion was something that either involved being violent or made him try to take much bigger risks than he knew he should. <br /> <br /> And that ends part one. I will probably have part two up by Sunday or Monday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T09:41:32-07:00","id":1403396,"title":"","content":"As always, great job with these posts. I really enjoy your take on these templates.<br /> <br /> I've been saving up my two cents for a little while, since none of the comments were interesting enough on their own.<br /> <br /> <u>Assamites</u><ul><li>The Gamester would have made a perfect Vizier.</li> <li>Psycho killer. Hmm, not bad in it's own right. As far as publishing history goes, though, this was past the point when developers should have said serial killers had been done, and writers should move on.</li> <li>I would like to have seen a Disparate who happens to be Assamite, but just wants get on with their own agenda.</li> </ul><br /> <u>Setites</u><ul><li>Weird personal note about the templates. Two of the drawings used looked exactly like people I know. No, really, like portraits. The dancer looked like a close friend in my gaming group. The closet setite looked like my best friend in college. In the Revised Setite clanbook, the guy who sells Egyptian tchotchkes looked a great deal like my boyfriend at the time. For a few years after the books came out new people in our gaming group... without prompting... would ask if we had won some sort of contest to be featured in a clanbook.</li> <li>The Gangsta. Umm, yeah. Bravo nature and demeanor. High strength and appearance. Low intelligence. I really want to believe the image of a scary, strong-backed, sexy, and stupid, Black man was just accidentally racist. But... damn.</li> <li>Path assignment is complicated by the fact that Path of the Warrior is one of the more under-utilized paths in the game. It's way more than just &quot;I hit stuff&quot;. If you believe in physical/spiritual dualism, the inherent corruptibility of the flesh, a mild degree of self-mortification, and the need to speed up Set's return, then Warrior works for you.</li> </ul><br /> <u>Tzimisce</u><ul><li>I am a big fan of the Tzimisce, especially Old Clan, but main clan, too. Yes, they became too fleshcraft-centric over the years, but there's a lot there to work with.</li> <li>What I am not a fan of is the asscrack art in this roach-covered porta-potty of a visual shitfest. (I had to tone down my reaction quite a bit. You just got the edited, calm version.) Okay, so I used to be a tattoo artist. I trained an apprentice once, and taught her how to work on skin that might be moving around or even jumping from time to time by having her draw while I drove her through an old parking lot with lots of potholes. No clipboards or flat surfaces were allowed; she had to draw on paper in mid-air. Her resulting linework was cleaner, neater and less painful to the eyes than this. The Tzimisce are a clan known for their fleshcrafting. It would have been helpful to have illustrations giving some idea of what that winds up looking like. Creating scribble-scribble sketches and turning them in as art doesn't make an illustrator daring or creative. It makes them look lazy and disinterested in finishing a project. Arghhhhh.</li> <li>I am going to go take a few deep breaths.</li> <li>Okay, I'm back. The Carnivorous Carny has a good reason to have unfocused abilities, he is pretty much a random embrace. An Archon stumbled into his house, and he somehow managed to stake him. Given the difference in power levels, this was mostly sheer luck.</li> <li>Similarly, the Count seems lackluster because he was embraced for one and only one reason: his pedigree. My only gripe is his being on Honorable Accord, when he is said to basically roll his eyes at the entire concept of the Sabbat.</li> <li>Torturer: Oh, look, somebody embraced a serial killer. That's novel and creative. Somebody should have thought of that before. Yawn.</li> <li>This book was the first (and, I think, last) time anybody mentioned how the mass embrace leads to Tzimisce who use their Vicissitude for the stuff most people would use it for: making their... ahem... bigger, and fixing their friends' bald spots. (&quot;Generation X&quot;, page 28) This was a delightful concept that never gets used. It would have been nice to have a template based on this. Maybe, a fashion model, body builder, or personal stylist? We saw a small glimpse of the possibilities in Revised's &quot;Star, Fucker&quot;.</li> </ul><br /> <u>Lasombra</u><ul><li>Why they're often Catholic? Beyond historical inertia, I always figured it was easier. When you infilitrate any of the thousand or so Protestant denominations you have to keep up to date with the different theologies and modes of worship. A newly arrived Lasombra working to infiltrate a Lutheran church had better know the difference between the Evangelical Lutheran Church of America, ELC in Namibia, Church of Norway, and Missouri Synod... including all the subtle, unwritten social traditions. Catholics, being simultaneously more centralized in doctrine and more culturally diverse, are simpler to research and blend into.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T11:46:07-07:00","id":1403406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1403396#post1403396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]What I am not a fan of is the asscrack art in this roach-covered porta-potty of a visual shitfest. (I had to tone down my reaction quite a bit. You just got the edited, calm version.) Okay, so I used to be a tattoo artist. I trained an apprentice once, and taught her how to work on skin that might be moving around or even jumping from time to time by having her draw while I drove her through an old parking lot with lots of potholes. No clipboards or flat surfaces were allowed; she had to draw on paper in mid-air. Her resulting linework was cleaner, neater and less painful to the eyes than this. The Tzimisce are a clan known for their fleshcrafting. It would have been helpful to have illustrations giving some idea of what that winds up looking like. Creating scribble-scribble sketches and turning them in as art doesn't make an illustrator daring or creative. It makes them look lazy and disinterested in finishing a project. Arghhhhh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of all the original clan books, Tzimisce has the worst art. Malkavian was full of crayon scribbles and Assamite was entirely photocopies of weapons, but at least their template art and full page chapter openings were done well. But almost nothing in Tzimisce is recognizably human and that's done on purpose. <br /> <br /> And I like the tattoo training story. I'm going to have to use that for something at some point. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T13:08:14-07:00","id":1403411,"title":"","content":"Man, this is a great thread! I keep thinking of stuff I want to agree with/disagree with/maunder into a senile digression about, but have been disciplining myself thus far... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1396463#post1396463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vicissitude power really took over the clan. Signature Disciplines often did that because they were the most distinctive things about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just boggled that so few (none, IIRC) of the signature characters had any focus on Animalism, at all. It's one of the big three Tzimisce disciplines, and modifying animal ghouls was a thing, so it could have easily been developed. But no, Vicissitude all the way, with a mild flirtation with Auspex. I remember a thread on the WW fora way back when asking 'what are the most creative things you can do with Vicissitude' and some wag quipped 'not take it?' Because *every* Tzimisce seemed to be all about it. (And every Lasombra about Obtenebration, when their clan's goals seemed to get vastly more potential usage out of Dominate, Presence, Auspex and / or Obfuscate, Obtenebration almost feeling like a point-trap, to keep you from being good at your job, in a way.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a result, when I ST my own Vampire chronicles, I don't use Vicissitude at all. I replaced it with standard Protean twenty years ago. None of my friends minded. None of them liked that Discipline anyway. It did mean I had to throw out much of the canon established around the clan and reinvent archetypes. But I thought the basics of the clan being territorial (as a result of their clan weakness), being &quot;fiends&quot; in the sense they relished tormenting the living, and that had remnant ties to feudalism - whether as being tied to estates or having &quot;serfs&quot; among the Revenants - was more than enough to create a strong clan identity. </div> </div> </div>Based on their strong ties to the ground / land / ancestral homes, I thought the original Viseratika (sp?) Discipline of the Gargoyle Bloodline, all about linking up to the walls and stonework of their warded places (and minus the gargoyle wings that came with it), was thematically far more suited to the Tzimisce than fleshcraft. Toss the fleshcraft into a popular path of their sorcery (along with weather control), and have their three Clan Disciplines be Auspex, Animalism and Viceratika. All about bonding to their territory, and it's creatures (and, through their magic, even influencing it's weather).<br /> <br /> As for the other clanbooks, in short.<br /> <br /> I remember liking the Malkavian Clanbook in all it's whackiness at the time, but after seeing the prominence of Fishmalks over the years, not so much.<br /> <br /> Clanbook Nosferatu was the best thing ever, at the time, and I remember being disappointed that the Revised edition's version didn't really match up. They were my favorite Clan for a time, because of that book.<br /> <br /> The Tremere somehow dodged being 'special sauced' quite so much as the other Clans with a special discipline, in that a couple of the sample characters didn't even have it, but focused on the perfectly cromulent Dominate and Auspex. I liked that. Although, IIRC, one of the characters writeups (Politico?) mentioned influencing things with a little blood magic, and had exactly bupkiss Thaumaturgy to back that up... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, those Setites. Another special sauce Clan that can do their actual thing much more effectively if they use disciplines like Auspex and Dominate, and avoid Serpentis like the plague. As the Evil Overlord's Handbook tells us, 'Turning into a giant snake never helps.' A better Path of the Warrior Setite example might have been cool.<br /> <br /> And the Assamites, so one-note. More focus on Vizier types or information brokers or middlemen who *don't* do the actual killing (but gather information on local kindred and maintain safehouses for visiting assassins) would have been neat.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","user":"Ian Turner","date":". 07-18-2020, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T06:40:45-07:00","id":1403520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1403396#post1403396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird personal note about the templates. Two of the drawings used looked exactly like people I know. No, really, like portraits. The dancer looked like a close friend in my gaming group. The closet setite looked like my best friend in college. In the Revised Setite clanbook, the guy who sells Egyptian tchotchkes looked a great deal like my boyfriend at the time. For a few years after the books came out new people in our gaming group... without prompting... would ask if we had won some sort of contest to be featured in a clanbook.[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that it's not so uncommon. Me, as a Brujah (I've been drawn with the coterie in V:tM revised quickstart) personally know count Vladimir Rustovich and Galliard template from 2nd edition Glasswalkers tribebook \ud83d\ude42.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 07-19-2020, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T14:29:51-07:00","id":1403573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1403411#post1403411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Assamites, so one-note. More focus on Vizier types or information brokers or middlemen who *don't* do the actual killing (but gather information on local kindred and maintain safehouses for visiting assassins) would have been neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember Clayton Oliver mentioning this as specifically why he made a lawyer specializing in contract law and negotiation one of the revised book's templates. Because, seriously, if everyone, even all the ghouls in training, are the assassins, who handles all the stuff like contracts, finances, safe houses, communications, weapons acquisition and maintenance, and a hundred other things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 07-19-2020, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T03:41:13-07:00","id":1403637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1403573#post1403573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember Clayton Oliver mentioning this as specifically why he made a lawyer specializing in contract law and negotiation one of the revised book's templates. Because, seriously, if everyone, even all the ghouls in training, are the assassins, who handles all the stuff like contracts, finances, safe houses, communications, weapons acquisition and maintenance, and a hundred other things?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be like in &quot;Day of the Jackal&quot; or &quot;Dogs of War&quot;, where the assassin/leader of mercenary team negotiate the terms, get the money and take care of other things by himself. On the other hand these books are set in the 60/70s and then, life of a mercenary was easier (vide Mike Hoare or Bob Denard).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 07-20-2020, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T11:23:54-07:00","id":1403692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1403573#post1403573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember Clayton Oliver mentioning this as specifically why he made a lawyer specializing in contract law and negotiation one of the revised book's templates. Because, seriously, if everyone, even all the ghouls in training, are the assassins, who handles all the stuff like contracts, finances, safe houses, communications, weapons acquisition and maintenance, and a hundred other things?</div> </div> </div> </div>That just goes back to the Assamites being an ill-conceived clan from the very beginning. They were intended to be a one note threat. The first edition clanbook was written with that in mind. So when they later wanted to expand it, they made even more bad decisions by the creation of the sub-clans that ultimately subverted the core concept. Today the clan is just a big hot mess from what I read about V5.<br /> <br /> The problems with Ravnos is mainly a problem with finding a good core concept. The problem with Assamites is that it was fine (a mysterious sect of assassins is a good hook), but too restrictive (and Quietus, like many of the Signature Disciplines, doesn't actually make sense as a coherent set of powers which is why V5 has messed with them).<br /> <br /> It would have been better if the writers had actually researched the clan's obvious inspiration - the real life assassins. The real world assassins didn't kill people simply because they wanted to kill people. They killed people who were a threat to them because they were an esoteric religious movement that was actively persecuted. Assassination was merely a side &quot;business&quot; that was an inadvertent result.<br /> <br /> If I had been in charge of the clan, I would have tried to duplicate that as best I could given the context of vampires and the game's history. So you need to make the Assamites believe in some really heretical/blasphemous thing that all the clans would persecute them for. I'm not sure what would be good, but it would have to be something fundamental - like an alternate set of traditions that permits the Assamites to act in ways the other clans can't accept. Something that directly threatened the other clans. Probably include something about Diablerie being OK, and even preferred since that fits the clan. I'm sure if I gave sufficient thought to it, I'd come up with something. Besides that, you need an esoteric interpretation of things - in other words, it's not the explicit reading of the text that reveals the truths. That is only for suckers. It's the hidden mean behind them. So they still look for a Book of Nod, but have completely crazy interpretations of it. So they're Noddist scholars as well, but their scholarly tradition is completely at odds with everyone elses. And create the clan culture around that. Make it really heretical, like if you didn't know a thing about VtM's mythology around vampirism and you had to come up with something new for a different game. Something that makes sense, but just doesn't fit (though the perfect thing would be to make sure the two contending myths had some elements in common so it is really a result of different interpretation and missing knowledge). And as a result, the early Assamites were despised and mistreated, and as a result they eventually struck back and started killing other vampires (though all the other clans say it was the Assamites who murdered them from the beginning, and their reactions were a result of that). That way you could explain the assassination function yet not have the clan be <i>defined</i> by it. They could have done this with the revised clanbook, but botched that up as well.<br /> <br /> I have never used the Assamites in any of my chronicles, but this is in my notes. So if I ever do introduce them as a plot element, I have something to work with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T11:49:13-07:00","id":1403695,"title":"","content":"I really like the Libellus Sanguinis castes that later were introduced in Revised. And I like even more the evolution of the clan, from one dimensional hassassins to complex followers of the code, they have become the judges, the guardians of the law and the bane of the infernalists. I like too the new iteration of Quietus, as a Blood sorcery. Quietus has not changed in the same way the lore of the clan did, this is the last step in a process to become playable. Although I prefer the Banu Haqim as anarchs (to not being in the same boat of the Tremere) and the Ministry as Camarilla, I am satisfied with them entering the major sects.<br /> <br /> About the templates, yesterday I take a look to the Ravnos Clanbook, due to this thread. And I even did not recognize the Cristopher Shy pre-tattoos art! If possible, I would like to know your oppnion also about the other characters depicted, Vassily Taltos and Ezmerelda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 07-20-2020, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T13:28:52-07:00","id":1403878,"title":"","content":"Anyone else ever feel like the Tzimisce's Clan disciplines aren't quite fitting? At least not with how the Clan was written up, including its templates? The Bratovich or Szantosa combinations made more sense to me personally.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T15:36:52-07:00","id":1404981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1403695#post1403695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the Libellus Sanguinis castes that later were introduced in Revised. And I like even more the evolution of the clan, from one dimensional hassassins to complex followers of the code, they have become the judges, the guardians of the law and the bane of the infernalists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the Libellus Sanguinis and revised clan book versions of the Assamites and Ravnos are leaps and bounds above their predecessors. Not least of which because if you actually liked the old versions, their still there, just now a minority within a much more diverse and well thought out group. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T15:42:56-07:00","id":1404982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1403878#post1403878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else ever feel like the Tzimisce's Clan disciplines aren't quite fitting? At least not with how the Clan was written up, including its templates? The Bratovich or Szantosa combinations made more sense to me personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially they are rural &quot;witches&quot;, with creepy psychic powers and command over the beasts of the earth (and to a certain degree other people's souls), plus accursed flesh-warping powers. I tend to view them as eldritch beings who put themselves apart from the lesser creatures that are humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T16:56:35-07:00","id":1404989,"title":"","content":"<b>Clanbook: Ravnos (part two)</b><br /> <br /> Finally, after an annoying delay.<br /> <br /> <b>The Dakini (False Prophet)</b><br /> So, curiously, this is one of the first instances of the clan being tied to India. This book presents it as being a tiny subset called the Vritra, but I still find it interesting in light of later developments. Anyway, this character is from the slums of Bombay (or Mumbai as it's called now) and had a knack for making herself useful as a beggar and runner, eventually working her way into the city's underworld. It's kind of implied that she probably spent some time as a prostitute, but thankfully doesn't focus or dwell on it, as she clearly managed to quickly become a victimizer rather than victim. Eventually she drew the attention of a vampire and was embraced. This helped get her foot into the world of high society, and the easy prey of gullible tourists. Then she decided that going to where the tourists came from might make for an even better hunting ground, so she relocated to North America (though you could just as easily make it the UK or Australia). Now she poses as an exotic Indian guru, offering made-up &quot;ancient wisdom&quot; in exchange for money and other gifts. Socials are primary, with Manipulation and Appearance at four. Dexterity is also at four, though I'm not entirely sure why. It feels like Mental might be more fitting as secondary. Streetwise and Subterfuge are both at three dots. Acting, Dodge, Animal Ken, Etiquette, Stealth, Linguistics, and Occult are all at two dots. Then there are a few single dots. Interestingly, none of them are in combat abilities, and if feels like its been a while since I've seen that. Disciplines include Animalism at two dots and Chimerstry at one. I kind of feel that one dot might've been better in Fortitude, but Special Sauce gotta Special Sauce, I guess. Backgrounds include Herd and Resources at five dots each, and once again it feels like it's been a while since I've seen anyone go all out on any backgrounds, let alone two of them. Retainers are three and Influence at two. Humanity is eight and Willpower is seven. I'm kind of surprised at how much I like this character. It feels like what the clan should be in a lot of ways. It totally avoids the The Rom stereotypes while foreshadowing the future rakshasa ideas. And her Cryme Tyme of Choice, &quot;deception&quot;, feels like something that's not going to stand out among the Kindred and risk turning into the Ravnos equivalent of a FishMalk.<br /> <br /> <b>The FX Artist (Lovable Goob)</b><br /> A life long geek obsessed with sci-fi, fantasy, horror, and especially the special FX techniques used to make genre movies. He was embraced by a Ravnos he saved from an anarch gang while working on a film set in LA. And that's pretty much it for back story (most of the word count is eaten up with shout outs to famous film names). He's almost entirely fixated on developing his grasp of Chimerstry and what he can create with it. His Cryme Tyme is &quot;trickery&quot;, as he enjoys fooling people, both with illusions and bluffs, which is sort of interesting, but really more than a little vague, and does have the down side of playing too heavily into FishRav territory. Mental is primary, with Intelligence and Wits at four each. Physicals are secondary, with Dexterity and Stamina at three. Charisma also gets a boost to three with some freebie points. Computer is at three dots, along with the secondary abilities of Disguise and Photography. Investigation, Occult, Repair and Security are are two each. He's also got a bunch of one dot abilities, including Acting, Firearms, and Science. Given his background and interests, you'd think Science might be a little higher. Also, his equipment lists explosives, but he seems to lack any ability relating to them. Disciplines are three dots in Chimerstry and, for reasons I can't fathom, a dot in Animalism. I could see a token showing in Fortitude, seeing as how LA is probably a rough place to live as a vampire, but nothing about him says Animalism. Backgrounds are two dots in Contacts, and one each in Generation, Mentor, and Resources. Humanity is seven and Willpower is six. I have mixed feelings about this character. One the one hand, I like that it has nothing to do with the The Rom or crime. And as a long time fan of old school practical FX work, I enjoy seeing it get a shout out. But I can't really escape the fact that this is a concept based entirely around the clan's Special Sauce power, which is a trope I've never been a fan of. If this had been a Toreador, I'd have loved the hell out of it. And the idea of having a compulsion for &quot;trickery&quot; sets off a few alarm bells. Still, as overall characters go, I think this is a fairly good one, though it could benefit from a little ability tweaking, I think.<br /> <br /> That's all for this one. Hopefully I can have the next part up before the end of the week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 07-29-2020, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T08:46:58-07:00","id":1405587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1404982#post1404982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essentially they are rural &quot;witches&quot;, with creepy psychic powers and command over the beasts of the earth (and to a certain degree other people's souls), plus accursed flesh-warping powers. I tend to view them as eldritch beings who put themselves apart from the lesser creatures that are humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about that too, and what came to mind was &quot;Auspex for telepathy and all that, Animalism as masters of base creatures... what's missing here is something like Dominate to make them true masters of their domains.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then I realised that's the Old Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T08:51:22-07:00","id":1405588,"title":"","content":"Also, something I never got about the Nosferatu. Both original and the revised Clanbook did it. The whole idea of Cleopatras, of taking beautiful people and turning them ugly out of spite. That's so often brought up, yet nowhere ever is one of the most natural results, I feel, properly explored: That trapping people in their own personal hells for eternity will make them resent you. Badly.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu should have a massive problem with childer killing their sires in revenge. How come there isn't a template for that? That makes for a PERFECT player character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26275,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","user":"Konigheim Horror","date":". 07-31-2020, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T16:04:07-07:00","id":1407197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1405588#post1405588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nosferatu should have a massive problem with childer killing their sires in revenge. How come there isn't a template for that? That makes for a PERFECT player character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have my copy of the book handy to check, but I recall that being the concept behind one of the vampire hunters in the original Hunters Hunted. A Nosferatu &quot;caitiff&quot; who was a wealthy industrialist embraced out of spite, now living as a total recluse and using his fortune to fund vampire hunters to go out and destroy all other kindred. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T16:09:45-07:00","id":1407198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1405588#post1405588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, something I never got about the Nosferatu. Both original and the revised Clanbook did it. The whole idea of Cleopatras, of taking beautiful people and turning them ugly out of spite. That's so often brought up, yet nowhere ever is one of the most natural results, I feel, properly explored: That trapping people in their own personal hells for eternity will make them resent you. Badly.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu should have a massive problem with childer killing their sires in revenge. How come there isn't a template for that? That makes for a PERFECT player character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is a likely result.<br /> <br /> However, once that happens, who else are you going to hang out with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T17:25:08-07:00","id":1407204,"title":"","content":"<b>Clanbook: Ravnos (part three)</b><br /> <br /> After a too long delay from work and feeling under the weather, which I apologize for. <br /> <br /> <b>The Seer (Ingenue)</b><br /> Oh boy, this character is one of the The Rom! ::sigh:: Buckle up, folks, this is going to be a bad one. So, to start with, her character quote is part of a tarot card reading. Because that's not at all stereotypical. She was born to the <i>Phuri Dae</i> &quot;family of power&quot; - one of the many terrible bits from World of Darkness: Gypsies (&quot;phuri dae&quot; more or less means &quot;grandmother&quot;, btw) - and possessed The Second Sight. So one night while her clan was traveling through Hungary, they were attacked by &quot;night walkers&quot; - Sabbat Gangrel - who were driven off by Ravnos vampires. As one of - maybe the sole, it's unclear - survivor, she was embraced. BTW, all of this heavily peppered with Roma jargon, all from a &quot;helpful&quot; lexicon section at the start of the book and repeating various stuff from WoD: Gypsies. She lost her Second Sight, but spontaneously developed Auspex instead. Exactly what she is currently doing as a vampire isn't really touched on at all. Mostly being a The Rom fortune teller, I guess. And best of all, as one of the The Rom, she doesn't have a Cryme Tyme of Choice. Instead, she simply ignores the rules of mulo vampire society, including the Traditions, because they don't apply to Ravnos. Yes, this &quot;The Rom Ravnos don't have a crime of choice because normal society rules don't apply to The Rom&quot; bit is one of the most scream-inducing bits of Dumb in a book that has more than its fair share of it. Anyway, Mental is primary, with Perception maxed out to five dots and Intelligence at three. Social is secondary with Charisma and Appearance at three. Empathy is at four dots, and Alertness, Linguistics and Occult are all at three each. Animal Kin and Investigation are both at two. Then there are a couple of single dot abilities. This includes one dot each in a trio of Lores: Gypsy, Kindred, and Lupine. This feels like a little bit of a waste. I've mentioned previously my feelings that if one is going to get a secondary ability, you may as well go whole hog and shoot for at least three dots in it. With Gypsy Lore, we get the bizarre occurrence of a character having to spend points to know about the culture she grew up in. Disciplines are Animalism at two dots, Chimerstry at one dot (because apparently it's a rule that everyone has to have it), and one dot in Aspex. I'm really not sure why the focus on Animalism. There's not really much in the back story to explain it. If anything, given the violent and brutal nature of her embrace, I'd have expected her to have Fortitude, and probably more than one dot of it. Backgrounds are two dots in Allies, and one each in Generation, Mentor, and Resources. Humanity is a whopping nine, and Willpower is seven. I'm mildly surprised she isn't on the Path of Paradox. The artwork thankfully avoids any sort of stereotypical Roma imagery. If anything, it looks vaguely Eastern European with a 90s club goer look. So, this isn't a great character. But it's not unsalvageable. If you excised all of the ridiculous material based on WoD: Gypsies and the face-palmingly bad &quot;The Rom don't have a crime of choice&quot; idea, I think you have the start of a decent idea. A young Roma woman who had minor psychic abilities whose family was murdered by vampires only to be saved by another vampire. And now she's forced to exist not only as a creature that is inherently unclean, but also the same sort of creature that killed her family. Which I think would have been fairly interesting. Especially if her &quot;criminal&quot; compulsion was to violate ethnic cultural taboos or to commit harm to other vampires (including herself). <br /> <br /> <b>The Smuggler (Criminal)</b><br /> Hmm. &quot;Criminal&quot; ... yes, I can see a lot of thought went into that concept. So, someone who grew up along the wharves of Amsterdam - which feels oddly specific - and quickly learned the ins and outs of the smuggling racket. And became very good at it, developing an international wealth of contacts. And so one night a Ravnos showed up on her boat and offered to embrace her and bring her into the &quot;real underworld&quot;. (I somehow suspect that this was less of an invitation and more of an offer you can't refuse.) And now she smuggles things for other vampires. And that's about it. We don't even get a Cryme Tyme, I guess because it's just the same smuggling she does all the time. Socials are primary, with a 3/4/3 split, and Mental secondary with 3/2/3. Alertness, Streetwise, Subterfuge, Drive, and Finance are all three dots. Firearms, Stealth, and Linguistics are two each. And then a couple of single dot ones. Noticeably absent is Bureaucracy, which would seem to be a necessary skill for someone who moves cargo around the world, something that usually requires a lot of paperwork. Disciplines are one dot in each, because there's just not a lot going on here. Though I can see how each might have its uses in this line of work. This is a background heavy character, with five dots in Contacts, four in Resources, two each in Influence and Retainers, and one each in Generation and Status. Humanity is six and Willpower is nine. The art is ... interesting. She's somehow giving off both Eurasian and &quot;Eurotrash&quot; vibes at the same time. She's also wearing a fishnet top that fully exposes both nipples, which are highly detailed. I think this is the first time we've had prominent partial nudity in a Clanbook, with even the Setite book avoiding it. Ironically, while the Tzimisce and Giovanni books were both released in sealed plastic bags marked &quot;adults only&quot; - one for that terrible image on the back cover and the other mainly for excessive strong language, casual racism and mention of incest - this one was not. I'm slightly curious how that happened. Overall, this character isn't terrible. But there's just not much there either. It's just sort of a vague and generic criminal based entirely around a specific crime. It feels more like an NPC rather than something you'd really want to play. <br /> <br /> That's part three. Tomorrow will be the final template and final thoughts. Then we'll be closing things out with Giovanni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T10:01:06-07:00","id":1407318,"title":"","content":"<b>Clanbook: Ravnos (part four)</b><br /> <br /> And the final part.<br /> <br /> <b>The Subway Conman (Bad Seed)</b><br /> So, a guy who grew up on the streets of New York, quickly mastering the ins and outs of various scams and confidence games, becoming a highly skilled professional at it as an adult. And then one night a vampire embraced him and now he continues to be a master con artist of the night. His Cryme Tyme is confidence games. I'm feeling a sense of deja vu here, perhaps because this is exactly the same thing as the previous Smuggler character, just with a different crime. It's like a formula: Grow up in rough neighborhood, become really good at the local crime, get embraced, become vampire criminal. At least he's not one of the The Rom, I guess. Mental is primary, with Wits maxed out to five dots and Perception at three. Socials are secondary, with Manipulation at four dots, and Dexterity is bumped up to three with some freebies. For abilities, Subterfuge is four dots, and Acting and Streetwise are three each. Drive and Stealth are at two. Then there's a scattering of single dots. Disciplines are, again, one dot of each. And again, I'm not really sure why he needs Animalism. You'd think a second dot in either of the other two powers would be more useful. Backgrounds are Generation at four dots, Resources at two, and Contacts at one. (I'm sort of surprised at the lack of an Ally or Retainer who could act as a partner/shill during certain cons.) Humanity and Willpower are both at eight. The art is fairly decent, what looks like your completely average nondescript city dweller from the 90s. This isn't a bad character by any means, but there's not a whole lot here either. It's very formulaic, especially coming right after another character built on the exact same formula. But as a basic cookie cutter &quot;grab and go&quot; premade character, it gets the job done. <br /> <br /> And that's kind of this whole group in a nutshell. Four of the seven are entirely based around a specific crime - serial killer, car thief, smuggler, conman - and that forms everything about them. And even the Dakini suffers from this to a degree. This is, I think, one of the problems the Ravnos had back then, and one they often share with the Malkavians. Some people will tend to look at their weakness/curse and build everything around it. The Carjacker, for example, starts from the idea that his crime of choice is stealing cars and just bases everything from that. But what if, instead, his criminal compulsion was to destroy the cars he steals instead of selling them? What if the Smuggler's compulsion was to betray her clients? What if the Con Artist kept feeling a compulsion to use violence instead of his wits? I think this would make for more interesting characters and roleplaying, but that's just my personal opinion. Out of all of these, the Dakini is probably my favorite, largely because it has nothing to do with The Rom and feels like someone engaged in standard vampire shenanigans rather than a specific crime picked from a list of felonies. I also kind of like the FX Artist for similar reasons, even if it is largely predicated on the clan's unique discipline. <br /> Representation wise, we have four men and three women. Only one of the women, the Smuggler, is really sexualized, mostly owing to that unfortunate fishnet top. The Dakini is Indian/South Asian, and the Carjacker is the only black character, which is unfortunate. And we have the Seer, who is The Rom. I'm actually grateful that only one of these played to the old ethnic stereotype of the clan. <br /> As far as what's missing, well, a Computer Hacker is somewhat surprising in its absence. Especially after seeing one in Brujah and in the Anarch Cookbook five years ago. (Not to mention having them in Glasswalkers and Artificers, and having an entire Mage faction based around the idea.) And as much as I'm happy to not have more stereotypical &quot;gypsy&quot; characters, I'm mildly surprised at the lack of some sort of militant activist/community guardian type. I know this flies in the face of how vampires would really be seen in Roma society, but given how heavy it was pushed in this and WoD: Gypsies, I find its lack of inclusion a little noticeable. <br /> The theme this book was apparently going for was Criminals, but I honestly feel a better theme for the Ravnos is that of Sin. People who are compelled to give into their worst vices and have to either struggle with that or just give up and roll with it. Or sometimes work very hard to justify them. But even if this was going for Criminals, two of them - the FX Artist and the Seer - don't really fit that. Which may be why this collection feels a little muddled and lacking focus. <br /> <br /> <br /> Next, Clanbook: Giovanni. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T16:27:14-07:00","id":1407395,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea: The story the Nosferatu tell themselves of their Founder was meant to be an allegory. &quot;If you take someone's beauty away forever, they will hate you and probably want to kill you. Don't do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, wouldn't it be funny if there were many more Ravnos around than people suspected, because one possible crime/sin they can be addicted to is cursing others to become undead, blood-drinking parasites? Ravnos randomly Embracing people would make them hated alright.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T18:48:50-07:00","id":1408623,"title":"","content":"<b>Clanbook: Giovanni (part one)</b><br /> <br /> Our final original clanbook, outside of the two made for Dark Ages (but that's another thread). Written in 1997 by Justin Hatch (who was at the time the Vampire: The Dark Ages developer IIRC and would soon go on the be Vampire: The Masquerade developer), and developed by Rob Hatch. Art for these templates is once again provided by Christopher Shy, so this does at least have a feel like these characters inhabit the same world as those in Ravnos. As I mentioned when talking about Tzimisce, this book also originally came in a sealed plastic bag marked &quot;adults only&quot;. This is mainly for issues of language, especially how casually racist, anti-Semitic, etc. the Giovanni tend to be. Because they are generally scum.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Justin Achille was very much a follower of pop culture and various materialistic trends, apparently relentlessly devouring magazines like GQ, Robb Report and other lifestyle publications. And this shows in how almost absurdly detailed each of these characters' equipment lists are. Ironically, this makes them incredibly dated. Where the early clan books have this sort of vaguely timeless &quot;alternate universe Bush Sr. administration/pre-digital age&quot; feel to them (something it shares with other period games like Nightlife, Cyberpunk 2020 and the like), this is very clearly a slice of real world 1997.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ingenue</b><br /> So this is someone who is probably from among the fringes of the main family. A fully Americanized upper class teen who only knew the extended family as being &quot;a little weird&quot; until after high school and she started being privately tutored by an older cousin instead of going to college. She excelled and was soon introduced to some of the &quot;more weird&quot; parts of the family, such as necromancy, and becoming a ghoul in what she thought was some sort of Black Mass ritual. By her late 20s, she was the successful director of one of the family's companies, and attracted the attention of the elders. That's when she learned that vampires are real. She's now wondering what other secrets the family is hiding. And one of those hidden things is that that are other vampires outside the Giovanni. So she has no clue any of the other Kindred exist, at least until she meets them in character. Which is kind of interesting. She's basically a balanced mix of intelligent, ruthless competence and stunning ignorance. Mental is primary with a 3/3/4 split, and Socials as secondary with 2/3/3. Alertness, Finance, and Investigation are all at three dots, and Empathy, Subterfuge, Drive, Etiquette, and Occult are each two dots. Then there are a few single dots, including Firearms which is her only combat ability. I personally would've dropped the single dot in Medicine and used it to raise Bureaucracy or Linguistics to two dots, but that's just my personal preference. Disciplines include Dominate at two dots, and Necromancy and Potence at one each, which seems fitting. (For some reason, every character has an extra Discipline dot bought with Freebies.) Backgrounds include three dots each in Allies and Contacts, one dot in Influence, and four dots in Resources. I'm not entirely clear on who her allies are, outside of the family. Humanity and Willpower are both six. All in all, this is a pretty good character. Admittedly there is a slight hurdle of trying to get her involved in any chronicle/coterie that isn't all Giovanni, but once that's out of the way, you have the interesting roleplaying challenge of being an already established and protected vampire who doesn't actually know anything about Kindred society. This could play out in a number of different ways, and I kind of like the idea of that. The only real problem with this character is the art. She is amazingly well drawn. And has this massive tattoo of a language/alphabet I don't recognize (and may not exist) going from her neck and up her face, including over her left eye. This is apparently the first sign of an obsession that would come to dominate Shy's artwork in the revised edition, and is just ridiculous on so many levels. Why any super successful business woman would choose to have that done is beyond me, and this is 20 years ago when the only people getting face tattoos were hard core body modders/urban primitives and even more hard core gang members. (A number of tattoo artists used to refuse to do that kind of work, which they called &quot;job killers&quot;, as it pretty much precluded you from ever getting any legit employment at the time.) And what makes me hate it all the more is that, if it wasn't there, this would be one of the best looking images in the book.<br /> <br /> <b>The Degenerate </b><br /> So, weirdly, this is almost the flip side of the previous character. Wealthy and super spoiled and even more super bored. Money could buy anything, she she wanted thrills that money couldn't buy, and found them in the family's perverse necromantic cult practices. But even this started to get a little dull when she realized that she wasn't going to advance much further because everyone knew she was only in it for perverted kicks. Then she stumbled on the fact that she could combine perversion to with necromancy to enrage ghosts into making unwise pacts with her (effectively teaching herself higher level necromancy powers). This apparently impressed some elders enough to embrace her. Now she continues her vile and self-centered existence in an eternal quest to stave off boredom, contributing to the clan only as much as she needs to. In essence, this is a really terrible person. (I'm mildly amused that this character predates anyone knowing who Paris Hilton was.) Socials are primary, using freebies to max Manipulation out to five, with Appearance at four dots and Charisma at two. Physicals are secondary with a 2/3/3 split. Subterfuge and Occult are at three dots each. Acting, Athletics, Empathy, Linguistics, and Medicine are at two each. Then there are several single dots, including Streetwise, Music and Investigation. Disciplines are Necromancy at three dots and Potence at one. Backgrounds include one in Allies, three in Herd (goth blood dolls), and four in Resources. Humanity and Willpower are both at five. This character is scum. And I mean that in a good way. She kind of encapsulates a huge chuck of the clan's overall corruption and can kind of serve as a mirror for the worst aspects of wider Kindred culture. I'm not sure I'd ever want to play this character, but she's at least memorable and interesting. I'll also give this write up a lot of credit for touching on a pretty cringe inducing sexual perversion but not overdoing it in excessive detail the way the Tzimisce ghoul revenant template did. The artwork isn't too bad. There are no tattoos - perhaps ironically, as this would seem to be the character most likely to have them - but her face seems to be lacking a certain amount of detail that most of the other templates do.<br /> <br /> That's all for now. Next will be part two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T19:03:50-07:00","id":1408626,"title":"","content":"Cb:Giovanni had some of my favourite artworks. The use of glowing white vampire eyes was great... which makes it even more frustrating that by the rules, almost nobody should have them and vampires can't see in the dark anyways. Ugh.<br /> <br /> It's telling the concept of The Degenerate made it into the clanbook the second time around as well, even if the actual characterisation was markedly different. This version managed to turn her vileness into something at least semi-useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T21:01:01-07:00","id":1408650,"title":"","content":"There were many good things about the Giovanni clanbook, but it had a major problem. Instead of being written as if the clan's human family is from northern Italian aristocratic stock with origins of being Renaissance princes (&quot;Modern Borgias&quot; as someone once wrote on these forums), the clanbook is written as if the clan is southern Italian born goomba mafiosos who belong on the Jersey Shore.<br /> <br /> It did a good job taking what was a one note clan and turning it into something that had more diversity within it, allowing more character concepts and such, and putting a lot of meat on the bones on the clan's history and secrets. (Though future writers would ignore some of the important facts contained in the clanbook - some of the minor families mentioned merely as providing &quot;breeding stock&quot; or mentioned that they had only a few vampires at all would suddenly become far larger as individuals would latch onto certain details they found compelling. This was a problem throughout the entire WoD line.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T23:38:31-07:00","id":1408657,"title":"","content":"Even being stereotypical and, in some ways, grossere and unfortunate, I loved this book. I printed all the templates and used them for a ready to play coterie long time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T12:54:18-07:00","id":1408770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1408650#post1408650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were many good things about the Giovanni clanbook, but it had a major problem. Instead of being written as if the clan's human family is from northern Italian aristocratic stock with origins of being Renaissance princes (&quot;Modern Borgias&quot; as someone once wrote on these forums), the clanbook is written as if the clan is southern Italian born goomba mafiosos who belong on the Jersey Shore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, part and parcel with Justin's obsession with pop culture was a habit of latching on to something that was trendy and not letting it go. In this case it was probably the movie Goodfellas. It probably also has something to do with why that one Scottish family effectively turned into the less likable characters from Trainspotting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T14:57:24-07:00","id":1408793,"title":"","content":"<b>Clanbook: Giovanni (part two)</b><br /> <br /> And once more into the depths.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Tomb Robber</b><br /> So, the first <i>Tomb Raider</i> game came out in 1996, and probably had a minor influence on this character. Namely the fact that its female and her equipment includes a pair of automatic pistols. There's also an obligatory Indiana Jones riff in the character quote. Anywho, she had a life long interest in archaeology and ancient cultures, as well as an awareness that real archaeology isn't like the movies. But she managed to become a fairly renowned published expert in her field, especially in thanatology. Eventually, she was offered a massive research grant, on the condition that she first undertake an expedition to Peru and bring back certain artifacts there. This eventually led to the embrace and now she travels the world (or at least the Americas; its a little vague here) hunting down ancient lore and relics that expand both her and the clan's understanding of Necromancy. She's a little atypical, personality wise, for a Giovanni, being pretty straight forward and forthright. Mental is primary, with a 3/4/3 split, and Physicals are secondary with 2/3/3 (taking advantage of being able to augment Strength with Potence). Socials go for a 3/1/2, making her pretty much what you see is what you get. She has the secondary ability of Archaeology at four dots. (The only character in the book with a secondary ability.) Security, Investigation, Linguistics, and Occult are all three dots. Alertness, Stealth and Survival are at two each. Combat skills are all at a single dot. Overall, a pretty competent character, extremely good at her niche but also able to apply those abilities in other areas. Disciplines are two each in Necromancy and Potence, both of which fit the character. Backgrounds are the bare minimum of five dots, with one in Allies, and two each in Contacts and Resources. I really think this is a character that could've justified a dot in Fame, given her background. Humanity is seven and Willpower is five. The art looks like that of your average everyday real world archaeology or eco-tourist. I find myself liking this character quite a bit. It plays very strongly with the clan's Necromancy focus, but in a way that doesn't hew to stereotype. She also feels like she could easily fit in with any mixed clan Coterie that has any sort of academic or Noddist leanings. If pressed to find a complaint, the only thing I can think of is that maybe she's too nice. But I suspect that might change after a century of age. <br /> <br /> <b>The Goodfella</b><br /> Speaking of stereotypes. So, yeah, its basically one of the guys from the movie of the same name. Well, not entirely. He's apparently from a Sicilian branch of the main Giovanni family (it doesn't specify if he's from Sicily or just his mortal family originates from there) that is heavily involved with the Mafia. He loved being in the Mafia as was good at it, eventually becoming a capo and being embraced. He holds to the old school ideas of honor and loyalty, perhaps more to the Mafia than to the Giovanni (perhaps because he doesn't really like being a vampire; this may have something to do with his having a wife and kids while alive, but what happened to them after his embrace isn't mentioned). He's a highly competent killer, but considers himself a professional and not a psychopath. Physicals are primary, with a 4/3/3 split, and Socials at secondary with 2/3/3. Brawl, Intimidation, Streetwise, and Firearms are three dots each, with Dodge and Melee at two. Then there's a scattering of single dots. Disciplines are one dot in Dominate, two in Potence, and then one in Celerity. Backgrounds include two dots in Allies, one in Contacts, four in Generation, and two in Resources. I presume Allies are the Mafia, and I once against find myself wishing that at some point there'd been something that looked in depth at what the different ratings for backgrounds like Allies, Retainers and the like could/should be for things like individuals, gangs, household staff and so on. Humanity is five and Willpower is nine. The artwork very seriously looks like it's Christopher Shy trying to mimic Tim Bradstreet's style, to the point where I could swear I've seen a very similar image on one of Bradstreet's covers for Hellblazer or The Punisher at some point. I have mixed feelings about this character. It's not a bad character by any stretch. But I can't escape the fact that it's based on a clan stereotype, and one that the author had repeatedly pointed out made little sense given the clan's Venetian origins. It feels like it's here to check off an item on a list and that's all. But once you move past that, it's a perfectly solid vampire character, and one who has some interesting loyalty conflicts. (Incidentally, I will note that there is a Venetian organized crime group known as <i>Mala del Brenta</i>, originating in the 1970s or so with local Veneto bandits, racketeers and smugglers organizing themselves in a fashion similar to the Mafia. They were actually supplying guns to Croatia when Yugoslavia fell apart, but were heavily cracked down on near the end of the 90s.)<br /> <br /> <b>The Cynical Bastard</b><br /> And from a pair who almost feel like normal Kindred, we move to this. A product of incest (at least it doesn't dwell on the details) and born incredibly ugly, he was never allowed to leave the house or interact with anyone outside the family. So he had two main hobbies, learning about necromancy and spying on everyone else in the house. And also r**ing all of his younger cousins. Because, sure, why not. At least he was constantly beaten for this. Which I'm not sure is much of an improvement. Eventually his &quot;uncle&quot; - the one that used to administer the beatings - made him a ghoul, and eventually a vampire. Of course, because of his misshapen appearance and lack of social skills, he'd almost totally dependent on his retainers to being him food. Basically, he hates his existence, hates himself, and hates everything else as well. Mental is primary, with Perception maxed out to five dots, Intelligence at three and Wits at two. Strength and Manipulation are both four dots. Dexterity and Stamina are two, while Charisma and Appearance are one. Alertness, Stealth, Bureaucracy, Investigation and Occult are all three dots each, and Brawl and Linguistics are two. The rest are single dot abilities, including Subterfuge, Firearms and Finance. Disciplines are one dot in each Clan affinity power plus an extra dot in Necromancy. Backgrounds are five dots in Allies, two in Generation, four in Resources, and two in Retainers. I'm forced to ask the question, who are his allies? Seriously, this is a character without even the slightest semblance of a friend at any time in his life, and who apparently doesn't even leave the house. This is also when I note that not a single one of these characters has a Mentor, not even ones like this one who've clearly been overseen by a vampire family member for much of their life. Anyway, Humanity is six (higher than the previous Mafia killer) and Willpower is four. The character image is of a heavy set older guy in a suit with his face largely obscured by cigar smoke. Contrast this with his equipment list, which includes &quot;sweatsuit purchased at Good Will.&quot; There seems to be a slight disconnect here. But overall, I'm not sure what the point of this character is, aside from an NPC masquerading (npi) as a premade PC. He really does nothing beside sit in his house all night stewing in his own misery and being a jerk. All the other characters go out and do things. This one doesn't even show any indication of that. He used to have an interest in studying Necromancy or in gathering information for his Uncle, but there's no indication he does either of those things anymore. So I'm just kind of at a loss here. <br /> <br /> That's it for part two. Next will be part three, with the final two templates and closing thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T19:52:31-07:00","id":1408836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1408793#post1408793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also when I note that not a single one of these characters has a Mentor, not even ones like this one who've clearly been overseen by a vampire family member for much of their life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've noticed this is a common problem in both many of the templates you've discussed in this thread, and in PC character creation. Players will mention stuff in their background that their character sheet does not support.<br /> <br /> One of my old GMs (long, long ago; in fact he was my first Vampire ST) would often give additional attributes based on character description so that the PC's stats reflected what the player said they were. This would always anger me because I always made sure my character sheet reflected my character background, and thus would lose out on build points compared to other players. I wonder how many other GMs and Players were in a similar dynamic where the GM would effectively give certain backgrounds or skills &quot;for free&quot; if something was in the character background, but not reflected mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 10-12-2020, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T20:14:00-07:00","id":1408839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1408793#post1408793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I can't escape the fact that it's based on a clan stereotype, and one that the author had repeatedly pointed out made little sense given the clan's Venetian origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually a LOT of the Giovanni clan's backstory as it developed doesn't make sense for a <i>Venetian</i> merchant family. While Venice was incredibly important to the Medieval economy and would remain rich for quite some time, being based on the Adriatic Sea and the eastern Mediterranean during the Age of Discovery meant the city as a whole declined in its great power status, and the reach of its merchants limited.<br /> <br /> Not only did it lack a connection to the Sicilian crime families well known in popular culture and connected to America, it had few dealings with the Atlantic trade, connection to the Spanish colonies, or the seaborne trade with the Orient. That eliminates not only the Putanesca, but the Dunsirn, Pisanob, Della Passaglia, Ghiberti, and other minor families.<br /> <br /> It's one reason why in my own chronicles I've moved the Giovanni family to Genoa, Venice's main commercial rival. Genoa actually had ties to Sicily and the Spanish/Portuguese colonial empires, and was represented much better in Western Europe and so could cultivate ties there with local merchants. It actually fits quite well, and eliminated all the problems I had with contradictions with history while preserving almost everything the clan had if based in Venice. <br /> <br /> I said the Giovanni family initially recruited the Putanesca as local strongmen in Sicily as a result of Genoa's support of the Crown of Aragon during the War of the Sicilian Vespers. Eventually as a result of long service, that family was rewarded with certain members being embraced; something that remained controversial within the clan. The Giovanni later became bankers that helped bankroll the Spanish crown during its Golden Age, and their merchant sailors helped the Spanish fleets explore and trade during the Age of Discovery, putting the Giovanni into contact with Mexico (the Pisanod), Angola (a Portuguese colony and major slave market - which the Ghiberti helped build), and Macau (where the Della Passaglia were based). Furthermore, even the timing of the Promise of 1528 fit well because that is the year the Genoan admiral of Spain, Andrea Doria, seized the city from occupation of the French. The Camarilla used the struggle between France and Spain for control of the city as leverage to force the Giovanni to accede to their demands, or risk being completely destroyed if the city was sacked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T15:08:09-07:00","id":1409020,"title":"","content":"Eh, I just see that as a feature of the Clan moving on and expanding its power base. The Ventrue aren't still in Babylon after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:15:13-07:00","id":1409200,"title":"","content":"The Ventrue (and every other clan) has a major advantage that the Giovanni don't - they don't restrict themselves to embracing only their own mortal descendants or their carefully selected lineages they marry into. They can quite easily send someone off to wherever, and they can start building a new powerbase. The Giovanni must grow organically in the sense they first need to make contact through their living relatives and only then embrace. Therefore, it makes more sense to see what are the natural paths for the mortal Giovanni to travel to and base themselves out of. <br /> <br /> (I also believe that having an established family/merchant presence in an area would make it much easier for the vampire Giovanni to expand and not be in violation of the Treaty of 1528. It's a much easier justification for them to say, hey, our mortal family already has a presence there, so we're sending a vampire to look after them. Prince of wherever, please let us into your domain. Rather than the clan sending someone to a place where they don't already have a presence, and thus have many more objections to overcome.)<br /> <br /> It just happens to be that all the areas where the Giovanni are supposed to go to don't map well to Venice, but they map very well to Genoa.<br /> <br /> So I made the change. It seems much more right to me. And it has the bonus of allowing me to figure out a lot of other details about the clan in my chronicles (like in what cities are they well represented; backstory behind some of the families; the other activities the clan and mortal family can be involved in).<br /> <br /> I'm sure 99% of players don't care. And that's fine. I wouldn't nitpick about it if I was playing in their games. But I think a base in Genoa makes much more sense than Venice, so I made the change in my own chronicles. And I can't see any negative to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T16:40:05-07:00","id":1409249,"title":"","content":"Venice has a rather curious history. (Thomas Madden's Venice: A New History is probably one of the better and more readable summaries of the city.) <br /> <br /> As for the Giovanni, I always just sort of assumed in my own head canon that they were, originally, Etruscan or thereabouts, and ended up mostly settled in the north around and above the Po River, and during the 7th century were one of the various extended families who fled into the lagoons and founded Venice. But there were probably a few minor branches still lurking around places like Rome, Noli, Ancona, and Genoa (but not Pisa, as they'd keep coming into conflict with their long time rivals/enemies, the Pallattino). <br /> <br /> Incidentally, given Venice's long connection to the Byzantine Empire and Constantinople, I'm kind of surprised in hindsight that there's no Greek family within the clan. Some old maritime family with a long history of smuggling, piracy, and weird old Chthonic rituals would be interesting, to me at least. <br /> <br /> Also, just because I wanted to, I decided that I wanted at least a couple of the families to be other Cappadocian families/cliques/cults who decided to throw in with Augustus and his coup. Hence, I've long had the Koenig be the remains of a Northern German Odinist cult who got into the iron-monger/arms dealer business early as a way to spread death and amass power. The other main one being a Portuguese faction whose name I invented and can't find my notes about them at the moment. After the Giovanni usurpation, they gradually incorporate the Rothstein's (Sephardic witches/necromancers), the Dunsirn (Scottish cannibals and smugglers), the Pisanob (Aztec priests), and the Milliners (Puritan witches turned early industrial mill owners), and a few others in the more modern era. But this is just because these include a lot of things I find interesting and enjoy playing around with (such as incorporating a bunch of Hawthorne, Lovecraft and King elements into the Milliners).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T17:43:20-07:00","id":1409253,"title":"","content":"<b>Clanbook: Giovanni (part three)</b><br /> <br /> And the grand finale.<br /> <br /> <b>The Doom Seer</b><br /> A child prodigy among a family deeply immersed in death, and from the sounds of things able to sense the presence of the restless dead even as an adolescent. He was given the embrace apparently before even leaving his teens. Already incredibly fatalistic, this didn't exactly improve his outlook any. He's a genius who sees life - as well as his own existence - as entirely meaningless, and works to hasten the inevitable end of all things. Mainly this seems to be motivated by a deep seated hatred of all the things he was denied in his own life. Mental is primary, with Intelligence maxed out to five dots, and Perception at three. Stamina is at four dots. Everything else is two. Occult is maxed out to five dots as well, and Linguistics is four dots. Alertness and Investigation are three each. Empathy, Subterfuge and Computer at two each. Then there's a scattering of ones, including Firearms, Medicine, and Science. Disciplines are all three dots in Necromancy, and a dot of Thaumaturgy bought with freebies. Backgrounds are one dot in Allies (again I'm wondering who/what this is), one in Generation, and three in Resources. Humanity and Willpower are both six. The art is perfectly fine. Almost nondescript in a way. I think this is probably a good choice. Too many times a character like this seems to get drawn as some sort of robed cultist or the like, so it's nice to see one that avoids that trope. Strangely, this character doesn't really illicit any strong reaction from me one way or the other. There's absolutely nothing wrong with him. But I'm not sure there's anything really standing out either. It's perfectly well written, but doesn't hook me the way a lot of other templates have. But for the life of me, I can't figure out why. He looks perfectly playable, even in a mixed clan coterie. But he's probably be on the bottom half of a list of such characters I'd want to play. <br /> <br /> <b>The Corporate Lick</b><br /> I'm kind of tempted to call this the black sheep of the family. He was the normal one of the bunch, and has always aspired to just fit in comfortably and not make waves or draw attention to himself. And for all his life, he was very good at it. Good grades, but not too good to stand out too much. A job with the family shipping business where he was competent but avoided unwanted attention. But apparently someone was paying attention because he ended up a ghoul and eventually embraced. Now he continues to do exactly enough work to not stand out as either incompetent or as exceptional. If he just keeps quiet and does his job, maybe he can survive. Mental is primary, with a 4/3/3 spread, and Physical secondary with 3/2/3. Acting and Alertness are three dots each. Drive, Etiquette, Bureaucracy, Computer, Finance, Investigation, Linguistics and Occult are all two dots. Empathy, Leadership, Subterfuge, Stealth, and Law are one each. Disciplines are two dots in Dominate, and one each in Necromancy and Potence. I kind of feel like this would probably be the one character who could do without any Necromancy, but I can also see where he'd learn the basics just to not stand out. Backgrounds are two dots in Allies (again, who/what?), two in Contacts, one in Influence, and four in Resources. Humanity is eight and Willpower is six. The art is exactly what you'd expect, and could do perfect double duty as a typical Ventrue. I find myself liking this character. He's very easy for me to empathize with, and feels like he'd have a lot of interesting internal conflicts during a chronicle, especially if part of a mixed coterie. And for a clan that, in its own way, is as screwed up as the various Tzimisce revenant families, he's refreshingly normal. <br /> <br /> And so those are the Giovanni. Overall, a fairly strong set. The strongest standouts, for me personally, would probably be the Ingenue (face tattoo aside), the Tomb Robber, and the Corporate Lick. The only really weak one is the Cynical Bastard. He just doesn't do anything but sit in his haven and stew in his own misery. The others are all perfectly fine. I just like those other three better. <br /> For representation, we have three women and four men. And none of the women are sexualized in the art (not even the Degenerate). However, they're all very white. I can mostly understand, given that with the exception of the Pisanob and Ghiberti, they're all very white families. Still, it would've been nice to see at least one character from one of those families as a Mesoamerican or half-African Giovanni. <br /> I'm honestly a little disappointed that there isn't some sort of parapsychologist character. Someone who takes a (quasi)scientific view towards necromancy, going out and investigating hauntings in order to capture ghosts for enslavement and locate places where the Shroud is thin so that the clan can buy them for future use in their efforts to tear it down. That and maybe some sort of creepy medical doctor type. <br /> I'm not sure there's really much of a theme here, save that of screwed up family dynamics and a general sense of trying to be hip by snarkily dismissing almost every aspect of the game and its setting. My own take has always been that the Giovanni are mostly about Corruption, be it moral, ethical, or spiritual. And most of these generally hold true to that, be it the slothful acceptance of the Corporate Lick, the greed for knowledge of the Tomb Robber, or the vile hate of the Cynical Bastard (or its cold counterpart in the Doom Seer). <br /> <br /> So, that's the final part of the final 2nd ed Clanbook. Next, will be closing thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T18:46:55-07:00","id":1414675,"title":"","content":"Fantastic write-up and I should have mentioned how much I appreciated this thread from the very beginning more often. Some parting comments.<br /> <br /> * I always figured the Giovanni were part of the Fourth Crusade since the sacking of Constantinople and the looting of that ancient city by Crusaders was driven by the kind of families the Giovanni are descended from. As such, they would have either wiped out the Greek branch of their family or had it destroyed by vengeful servants of Michael.<br /> <br /> * I am surprised that there's not more literal color in the faces of the Italian branches of the family. One of the interesting things to happen to Helena Bertinelli (Huntress of DC comics) was that when 52 was announced, they went for a more classic Sicilian appearance and many fans complained, not realizing that they're often a little browner than pure pale skin.<br /> <br /> * I generally view the Treaty of 1528 as consisting of a variety of loopholes that both the Giovanni and Ventrue are aware of. For me, the basics are that the Giovanni will never hold any title in the Sabbat or Camarilla or rule any cities themselves. They're welcome(ish) at Elysium and can be accepted by Princes to build up their mortal holdings but the Jyhad is off-limits. This is, of course, nonsense and they're heavily involved but just staying indirect is it's own reward to many Ventrue.<br /> <br /> * This is purely headcanon but in my games, Augustus Giovanni is not as omnipotent as other Antediluvians. I stated in my games that Augustus has only 1 Level 10 Discipline and that is a Dominate 10 that allows him to dominate any one of his blood descendants or family by marriage in the world. Which is why the clan has it's weird...quirk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T22:44:11-07:00","id":1420081,"title":"","content":"I feel it is one of the greatest mistakes of tabletop RPG there wasn't a Setite or Giovanni archetype for Professional Wrestler based on the Undertaker.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1070084370696794112/ecpXIUeY_400x400.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I was just thinking about the fact that he was at his most bizarre in the late Nineties and it would have been one of the most played Character Templates, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not sure which Clan suited him better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T12:59:55-07:00","id":1420164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1420081#post1420081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it is one of the greatest mistakes of tabletop RPG there wasn't a Setite or Giovanni archetype for Professional Wrestler based on the Undertaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that both Rob Hatch and Justin Achilli (as well as Ethan Skemp and Ken Cliffe) were big pro-wrestling fans back then, it's slightly surprising that there isn't. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, funny tangentally related story. One Monday night way back then, I'm hanging out on an IRC chat with a number of people including Richard Dansky while at the same time watching WWF Raw is War (as it was known back then) and WCW Nitro, when WWF debuts their new wrestler, Gangrel. For those that don't remember, he had a vampire gimmick. A very blatant one. (I would find out later that he used to do the independent circuit under the name of &quot;The Vampire Warrior&quot; or something like that.) Gangrel is a name he only used in the WWF, and the word doesn't really have any connection to vampires outside of White Wolf. I mention this to Rich, and he says &quot;yeah, I just got phone calls and emails from half the office about it.&quot;<br /> If you go back and watch Gangrel's matches from those next couple of weeks, you'll notice that Jim Ross and Jerry Lawler are always very careful to avoid describing him as a vampire, or the &quot;red liquid&quot; he drinks from a chalice before spit-spraying it everywhere as blood. I was later told that White Wolf's legal representation had contacted the WWF about it the next day. This eventually worked out into a deal in which, as I understand it, they could use the Gangrel name in exchange for, IIRC, mostly some free advertising in WWF's magazine. Given that at the time, WWF's audience was a few orders of magnitude above that of any RPG company, it probably wasn't that bad of a deal. But, ironically, this may partially explain why of everyone in the eventual Brood faction, Gangrel had the shortest run with WWF and was never pushed very much, especially after Edge and Christian were split off and pushed to the moon as a tag team. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T09:36:35-07:00","id":1420696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1420164#post1420164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that both Rob Hatch and Justin Achilli (as well as Ethan Skemp and Ken Cliffe) were big pro-wrestling fans back then, it's slightly surprising that there isn't. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, funny tangentally related story. One Monday night way back then, I'm hanging out on an IRC chat with a number of people including Richard Dansky while at the same time watching WWF Raw is War (as it was known back then) and WCW Nitro, when WWF debuts their new wrestler, Gangrel. For those that don't remember, he had a vampire gimmick. A very blatant one. (I would find out later that he used to do the independent circuit under the name of &amp;quot;The Vampire Warrior&amp;quot; or something like that.) Gangrel is a name he only used in the WWF, and the word doesn't really have any connection to vampires outside of White Wolf. I mention this to Rich, and he says &amp;quot;yeah, I just got phone calls and emails from half the office about it.&amp;quot;<br /> If you go back and watch Gangrel's matches from those next couple of weeks, you'll notice that Jim Ross and Jerry Lawler are always very careful to avoid describing him as a vampire, or the &amp;quot;red liquid&amp;quot; he drinks from a chalice before spit-spraying it everywhere as blood. I was later told that White Wolf's legal representation had contacted the WWF about it the next day. This eventually worked out into a deal in which, as I understand it, they could use the Gangrel name in exchange for, IIRC, mostly some free advertising in WWF's magazine. Given that at the time, WWF's audience was a few orders of magnitude above that of any RPG company, it probably wasn't that bad of a deal. But, ironically, this may partially explain why of everyone in the eventual Brood faction, Gangrel had the shortest run with WWF and was never pushed very much, especially after Edge and Christian were split off and pushed to the moon as a tag team. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember him too. It's sad that he had such short career. I wonder, considering Edge's return, how Vince McMachon would react if Gangrel Embrace one of the &quot;youngbloods&quot; from WWE NXT \ud83d\ude09.<br /> <br /> It also explains the existence of Luchador from Nosferatu clanbook and the entire Extreme Wrestling Warfare in cWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T10:05:25-07:00","id":1420701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1420081#post1420081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it is one of the greatest mistakes of tabletop RPG there wasn't a Setite or Giovanni archetype for Professional Wrestler based on the Undertaker.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1070084370696794112/ecpXIUeY_400x400.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I was just thinking about the fact that he was at his most bizarre in the late Nineties and it would have been one of the most played Character Templates, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not sure which Clan suited him better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that neither of them. It would be too obvious (like mamy templates IMHO). But I like Luchador template from Nosferatu clanbook and Gangrel in real life. My own idea for a vampire wrestler would rather be a Toreador based on Shawn Michaels as Heartbreak Kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T14:55:21-08:00","id":1425251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1396447#post1396447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Clanbook: Tzimisce (part one)</b><br /> <br /> Once again back to 1995. This book was written by Rob Hatch, who would go on to be Vampire developer for a while, and you may remember as the author of the Nosferatu book. Art is by John Cobb, who has a rather distinctive art style, in which I mean that almost none of it looks even remotely human or natural (and in some cases this includes even allegedly human looking characters seeming to have distorted features and/or anatomy). And almost every humanoid image in the book has these crazy bug eyes like they are rolling around in the creatures' heads. The only human looking image in this entire book is the cover image by Tim Bradstreet (which is pretty good, if totally at odds with the tone of the rest of the book; it kind of looks like a young version of Rob Zombie's wife). And I think the back cover image is the only one to rival that of the Malkavian nose-picker in the &quot;what were they thinking?&quot; category. I'm actually going to trigger warning this one.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's a face that's been remade into a vulva/vagina with teeth. The &quot;nose&quot; is a clitoris, and is pierced, because of course it is.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> This book was originally shipped in a plastic back with &quot;Adults Only&quot; printed on it, and a black square blocking said image on the back.<br /> This book was developed by Jennifer Hartshorn, who during her tenure at WWGS was developer for Wraith, Vampire: The Dark Ages and Vampire at various points.<br /> As I mentioned, this is clearly the point when the clan shifted from &quot;slightly respectable creepy weirdoes&quot; to &quot;all out freak show&quot;. This is not exactly helped by what I've come to notice as a trend of &quot;shock for shock's sake&quot; aspect of Hatch's work, especially when dealing with the Tzimisce. While I think grotesque certainly has its place in Vampire, I think this tends to over do it a bit. Some of it starts to feel like it's just &quot;look how edgy and adult I am for talking like this/about this subject&quot; adolescent posturing. And I can't help but roll my eyes at it when it pops up.<br /> These character use the Sabbat character sheet, with its paths and alternate virtues, but still have the standard character creation guidelines at the bottom. Unlike all of the previous ones, it doesn't have the clan Disciplines typed out on the sheet, instead having them written in. (This is weird as the four page sheet in the back actually has those.) Also, this is back when the Tzimisce and Lasombra lacked their own clan symbol, just having the Sabbat wax/blood seal with a T instead of an S. And all of these have a completely different concept written on the character sheet than what they are titled as. I find this a little annoying.<br /> <br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks a lot for this article, I am preparing a review for the Clanbook Tzimisce and I found it very inspiring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T13:05:39-07:00","id":1456903,"title":"","content":"Apologies for any thread necromancy, but is there a chance of revisiting this topic with the templates for the Revised Clanbooks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T18:32:41-07:00","id":1456920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1456903#post1456903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for any thread necromancy, but is there a chance of revisiting this topic with the templates for the Revised Clanbooks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though I am likely to do it as a new thread, and it would also likely come after one about the Vampire: The Dark Ages ones (which would likely come after a second edition Werewolf one in all honesty). The single biggest issue is time, as I'd originally done this during lockdown, so future efforts are likely to be a lot slower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T08:50:25-08:00","id":1527842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1390159#post1390159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's essentially the archetypical Serpent of Light, and is competently built as such. And I swear that the character art reminds me of a specific rap/hip hop artist from the very late 80s/very early 90s, I just can't for the life of me remember who.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time I see the art for the Serpent of the Light Mystery Man, with his oddly small head (and hands), all I can think of is the shrunken head guy in the Beetlejuice waiting room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7749-ibnshisha","name":"IbnShisha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}